cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FDA novel drug approvals and market withdrawals by therapeutic modality, 1990-2025"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23017496"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23017495"
    description: "Concept DOI - always resolves to the latest version of this dataset"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
abstract: >-
  Year-by-year classification of 1,246 novel active substances approved in the United
  States between 1990 and 2025 into seven therapeutic modalities (small molecule,
  antibody, antibody-drug conjugate, peptide, protein/enzyme, oligonucleotide, other),
  with a companion curated set of 45 US market withdrawals classified on the same scheme.
  Built from a frozen Drugs@FDA snapshot, cross-referenced against ChEMBL, and reconciled
  against FDA's published novel drug approval counts for 2006-2025 (r = 0.9992).
keywords:
  - drug approvals
  - therapeutic modality
  - biologics
  - FDA
  - pharmaceutical innovation
  - drug withdrawals
